# D18 — port the GC9503V WVGA LCM (display fix — dark-screen close)
# Spec: hermes-release-plan hard gate ("display must-preserve"), bob-m2-spec OQ-7.
# Task: .specs/forge-d18-task.md; audit trail: .specs/forge-d18-report.md.
#
# Donor search outcome (task step 1): NO public tree carries a gc9503v_wvga_dsi_vdo
# LCM driver. Checked: bq/aquaris-E5FHD and CyanogenMod/android_kernel_mediatek_sprout
# (task's named donors — both lack gc9503 entirely, cloned+grep'd in-tree), the full
# git trees of persimmon/oxygen/motorola/selene (git ls-tree grep — no hits), plus
# grep.app, Sourcegraph global (incl. archived+forks), searchcode, DuckDuckGo and
# GitHub issues for the exact driver names — 0 hits everywhere (see report S1).
# The only public GC9503V implementation in this ODM's lineage is SchulzCode/Y2Linux
# @ c53427ae (GPL-2.0, Innioasis Y2 "eastaeon82_wet_kk" MT6582 board = the Q5's
# factory family): its panel.c pins down the vendor contract — DCS 0x04 = xx 95 03/04
# ID rule, 0xF0{55 AA 52 08 00} unlock block, gamma rows 0xD1..0xD6, the
# reset-high/low/high init pulse and the suspend epilogue that leaves reset HIGH
# 50 ms (donor pinned as donors/y2linux/kernel/platform/panel.c). Its documented
# "two panels in one product" hazard (GC9503V vs ST7701S across units) is handled
# here the way BOTH the Q5's LK and the Q5's kernel handle it — see wiring below.
#
# The port's authoritative data is the Q5's own pinned Lithium kernel blob
# (5217dd41…, decomp d284ba16…): the compiled gc9503v_wvga_dsi_vdo_hsd +
# gc9503v_wvga_dsi_vdo_boe LCM drivers were decoded symbol+datawise (LCM_DRIVER
# structs @0xc0b8c9fc/0xc0b8f184 on this tree's exact lcm_drv.h layout;
# lcm_driver_list @0xc0b8a458 = {st7701_ivo, st7701_dingsj, hsd, boe}; init tables
# 49 + 43 rows and the shared 39-row suspend table @0xc0b8bf04/@0xc0b8e68c — the
# tables tile the blob's rodata with zero gaps; LCM_PARAMS = this tree's layout
# minus the od_table tail; compare_id = DCS 0x04 3-byte read, hsd accepts
# 0x9503/0x9504, boe 0x9505/0x9506). Ground truth for the name contract: the Q5's
# own preboot LK (pinned as donors/lk-q5.bin, sha a9b556db… = the recovery-base
# MANIFEST lk.bin = Manufactory_latest/appsboot.raw) carries exactly
# {gc9503v_wvga_dsi_vdo_hsd, gc9503v_wvga_dsi_vdo_boe, st7701_wvga_dsi_vdo_ivo,
# st7701_wvga_dsi_vdo_dingsj} and passes "%s lcm=%1d-%s" at boot.
#
# WIRING DEVIATION from task step 3 (documented, per-blob ground truth): the task's
# literal CONFIG_CUSTOM_KERNEL_LCM="gc9503v_wvga_dsi_vdo" cannot name a real driver
# — the Q5 blob compiled the _hsd/_boe SUFFIXED names only, and disp_get_lcm_name_boot()
# sets isLCMFound=1 for ANY non-empty name after "lcm=?-"; a no-match leaves
# lcm_drv=NULL and SKIPS compare_id auto-detect → the exact dark screen being fixed.
# The evidence-locked wiring is BOTH blob names, exactly as the vendor build did;
# a bare-name driver could never exact-match the LK's strings. (st7701s names are
# out of scope per the task's gc9503v pin; flagged as a boot-log-gated follow-up.)
# CONFIG_LCM_HEIGHT/"800">/WIDTH/"480" are untouched (blob get_params: 480x800).
#
# Parity gates (build/61_kernel_delta_lcm.sh): gc9503v strings in, hx8369b gone,
# D1..D17 sets intact (gsl_tp 19 / ccci 750 / mali 809 / aw87559 3 / dw9714 28 /
# dw9719 53 / FGADC 24 / gc5004 2 / hi253 6 / hi704 7 / mt6323 19 / kpd 1 / auxadc 210).


--- /dev/null
