+ * Structure follows the in-tree hx8369b_wvga_dsi_vdo_tinno LCM driver (same
+ * LCM_DRIVER registration signature).  Every hardware byte is evidence-locked
+ * to the pinned Lithium kernel blob (5217dd41…, decomp d284ba16…) — the only
+ * blob known to drive this panel — and to the Q5's own preboot LK
+ * (donors/lk-q5.bin), which passes "lcm=%1d-<driver .name>" to the kernel.
+ *
+ * Ground truth (VA trail in .specs/forge-d18-report.md):
+ *   LCM_DRIVER gc9503v_wvga_dsi_vdo_hsd_drv        VA 0xc0b8c9fc (blob .data)
+ *   lcm_driver_list[]                              @VA 0xc0b8a458 =
+ *       { st7701_ivo, st7701_dingsj, gc9503v_wvga_dsi_vdo_hsd, gc9503v_wvga_dsi_vdo_boe }
+ *   lcm_get_params                                 VA 0xc03d0f64
+ *   init/resume push_table                         @VA 0xc0b8b13c (49 rows)
+ *   suspend    push_table                          VA 0xc0b8bf04 (39 rows, identical
+ *       for both variants); init+suspend tables tile the blob's rodata with zero
+ *       gaps straight into the next LCM_DRIVER struct.
+ *   compare_id: DSI read of DCS 0x04 (3 bytes) = 0x9503/0x9504(this variant).
+ *   Cross-check donors: SchulzCode/Y2Linux (Innioasis Y2, same eastaeon/
+ *   innioasis MT6582 lineage) documents the same vendor contract for GC9503V:
+ *   "0x04 = xx 95 03/04", the 0xffe-delay/0xfff-end table encoding, the same
+ *   0xf0 {55 aa 52 08 00} unlock block and gamma rows 0xd1..0xd6, the
+ *   reset-high 10ms/low 10ms/high 120ms init pulse and the suspend epilogue
+ *   that leaves reset HIGH for 50 ms — all re-derived here from the Q5 blob
+ *   itself, whose bytes are authoritative for THIS panel.
+ *
+ * The _hsd variant (GalaxyCore GC9503V, Hansong-packaged panel) answers
+ * DCS 0x04 with 0x9503/0x9504; the _boe sibling (BOE-packaged panel of the
+ * same IC family) answers 0x9505/0x9506 and ships as separate LCM dir/Makefile.
+ * The vendor blob built BOTH into lcm_driver_list in this order, precisely so
+ * that whatever the device's LK names at boot exact-matches
+ * disphal_get_lcm_driver()'s strcmp — with a name mismatch the MTK boot flow
+ * pins isLCMFound=1 and skips compare_id auto-detect, leaving the screen dark.
+ */
